--------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. SOURCE CODE — CLOSED UNTIL MAINTENANCE DORMANCY
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

The inkField source code, shaders, embedded scripts, and binary assets
in this repository are not yet open for redistribution, modification,
or derivative works. This restriction is a transitional state — when
the author steps back from active maintenance, the full source will be
re-licensed under an OSI-approved open-source license so the community
can continue it freely.

Until that day:

You ARE welcome to:
  - View and clone the repository for personal study.
  - Use the published web application for any purpose, including
    creating artworks for sale:
    https://ileivoivm.github.io/inkField/
  - Submit paintings to the public gallery.
  - File bug reports, feature requests, and documentation PRs.

Please don't (without prior written permission):
  - Redistribute the source code, in original or modified form.
  - Publish a fork as a standalone product.
  - Integrate the rendering engine into another application.
  - Create a derivative codebase from `script.js` or `shader.js`.

If you want to do any of the above for research, collaboration, or a
specific project, please just ask: ileivoivm@gmail.com. The default is
"not now," but the door is open.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------
2. ARTWORKS CREATED WITH INKFIELD
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

Paintings you create using inkField — the JSON recordings, rendered
frames, and resulting images / videos — belong to you:

  - Full copyright belongs to the creator.
  - Commercial use is expressly permitted: exhibit, sell, mint as NFT,
    license, or distribute without restriction.
  - No royalty or revenue share is owed to the inkField project.
  - Attribution ("Made with inkField") is appreciated but not required.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------
3. GALLERY SUBMISSIONS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

By submitting a recording to the public gallery under
`gallery/recordings/`, you grant the project a non-exclusive,
royalty-free license to host, display, and reference your submission
for gallery purposes. You retain full copyright. You may request
removal at any time by filing a GitHub Issue.

